Subject: sound: decode Ogg Vorbis to host byte order (big-endian hosts played
 noise)

ov_read was always asked for little-endian samples, but OpenAL reads its 16-bit formats in host order, so on a big-endian machine every sound was white noise. This is the only ov_read and the only raw PCM handling in the client's sound code.

diff --git a/src/client/sound/ogg_file.cpp b/src/client/sound/ogg_file.cpp
--- a/src/client/sound/ogg_file.cpp
+++ b/src/client/sound/ogg_file.cpp
@@ -161,7 +161,12 @@ std::optional<OggFileDecodeInfo> RAIIOggFile::getDecodeInfo(const std::string &f
 RAIIALSoundBuffer RAIIOggFile::loadBuffer(const OggFileDecodeInfo &decode_info,
 		ALuint pcm_start, ALuint pcm_end)
 {
-	constexpr int endian = 0; // 0 for Little-Endian, 1 for Big-Endian
+	// ov_read: 0 for Little-Endian, 1 for Big-Endian. OpenAL reads AL_FORMAT_*16 buffers in host order.
+#if defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && defined(__ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__) && __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+	constexpr int endian = 1;
+#else
+	constexpr int endian = 0;
+#endif
 	constexpr int word_size = 2; // we use s16 samples
 	constexpr int word_signed = 1; // ^
 
